{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>To Him who smote</b> — 'and killed.' The meaning is doubled, and now he specified them because they were mighty. So too the prophet said concerning the Amorite: 'who were as tall as cedars, lofty and strong as oaks' — and likewise: 'I delivered the Amorite by my sword and by my bow,' for the iniquity of the Amorite was not yet complete."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 136, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:41:53.075608300Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}